WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.941 --> 00:00:15.222
someone shouted from outside.

2
00:00:15.242 --> 00:00:16.884
"Come and look!"

3
00:00:17.844 --> 00:00:19.666
The Skellians headed for the door of the hut.

4
00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:21.988
"What are we going to do?"

5
00:00:22.268 --> 00:00:22.929
Gliss whispered.

6
00:00:22.949 --> 00:00:26.472
"We can't get back to Magica without a wormhole!"

7
00:00:26.492 --> 00:00:31.576
"We'll figure something out," Zann said, trying to sound confident.

8
00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:35.274
Zann and his friends joined the Skellians at the doorway.

9
00:00:36.214 --> 00:00:37.595
Everyone was staring at the beach.

10
00:00:37.615 --> 00:00:39.397
"What's going on?"

11
00:00:39.697 --> 00:00:40.617
Perda asked Ello.

12
00:00:40.637 --> 00:00:42.399
"It's the gulpers."

13
00:00:42.879 --> 00:00:43.479
Ello pointed.

14
00:00:43.499 --> 00:00:45.260
"They're clustering along the shore!

15
00:00:46.121 --> 00:00:48.162
It's weird—they don't usually do that."

16
00:00:48.963 --> 00:00:50.324
Zann squinted through the rain.

17
00:00:51.264 --> 00:00:54.006
Several gulpers were splashing around in the shallows.

18
00:00:55.147 --> 00:00:57.949
A few Skellians climbed down the rope ladder for a better look.

19
00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:01.371
"Isn't it dangerous to get too close to those things?"

20
00:01:01.751 --> 00:01:02.332
Gliss asked.

21
00:01:03.124 --> 00:01:04.686
"It's okay," Ello replied.

22
00:01:04.706 --> 00:01:06.747
"The gulpers can't come onto land.

23
00:01:07.148 --> 00:01:07.868
Let's take a look!"

24
00:01:08.729 --> 00:01:11.952
Following Ello, Zann and his friends climbed down to the beach.

25
00:01:12.853 --> 00:01:15.295
That seemed to make the gulpers even more excited.

26
00:01:16.136 --> 00:01:19.439
They churned up the water so much that part of the beach was flooded.

27
00:01:19.459 --> 00:01:24.944
"It's because of our visitors," a woman said, staring at Zann and the others.

28
00:01:24.964 --> 00:01:29.248
"They must give off enough magic energy to attract the gulpers."

29
00:01:30.348 --> 00:01:32.330
"Good thing they can't come on land."

30
00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:33.631
Gliss sounded nervous.

31
00:01:33.651 --> 00:01:36.653
"Be careful, Darb!

32
00:01:37.114 --> 00:01:38.355
Don't get too close!"

33
00:01:39.455 --> 00:01:40.196
Zann smiled.

34
00:01:40.216 --> 00:01:44.520
"Darb is always curious about new creatures," he told Ello.

35
00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:48.122
"I think that's the same gulper that bumped our raft."

36
00:01:48.943 --> 00:01:50.404
Darb pointed to one of the creatures.

37
00:01:50.965 --> 00:01:53.787
"See? I recognize its color and the shape of its eye."

38
00:01:53.807 --> 00:01:57.130
"If you say so," Perda said dubiously.

39
00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:59.632
"They all look the same to me."

40
00:02:00.736 --> 00:02:04.278
"I can't see anything in all this rain," Gliss complained.

41
00:02:05.299 --> 00:02:07.700
Snapping her fingers, she conjured up an umbrella.

42
00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:11.222
That caused the gulpers to go into a frenzy.

43
00:02:12.323 --> 00:02:14.724
One even flopped onto the beach, splashing everyone.

44
00:02:16.245 --> 00:02:17.625
"Wow," Zann said.

45
00:02:17.645 --> 00:02:21.047
"They definitely noticed that magic you just did, Gliss."

46
00:02:21.067 --> 00:02:25.010
"Yeah." Perda stared at the gulpers with amazement.

47
00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:30.496
"It's almost like we're having our magic tracked by Morb again!"

48
00:02:30.516 --> 00:02:35.760
Until that moment the Skellians had been laughing and pointing at the gulpers, seeming to enjoy the unusual

49
00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:39.743
spectacle. But at Perda's comment, they all became silent.

50
00:02:39.763 --> 00:02:41.944
"What did you say?"

51
00:02:42.304 --> 00:02:43.445
one of the women asked Perda.

52
00:02:44.386 --> 00:02:45.386
Perda looked confused.

53
00:02:45.407 --> 00:02:47.988
"What? You mean about Morb?

54
00:02:48.909 --> 00:02:50.650
He's just this guy from Magica.

55
00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:56.274
It's a long story, but I guess we could tell you The Skellians traded serious glances.

56
00:02:56.294 --> 00:02:59.156
"I'm sorry," an older man said.

57
00:02:59.956 --> 00:03:03.097
"I'm afraid we cannot welcome you into our village after all.

58
00:03:03.337 --> 00:03:04.197
You'll have to leave."

59
00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:06.978
"What?" Perda exclaimed.

60
00:03:06.998 --> 00:03:08.858
"Where are we supposed to go?

61
00:03:09.879 --> 00:03:12.159
You just told us there's hardly any land here!"

62
00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:13.740
The man shrugged.

63
00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:18.981
"I'm sorry," he said again, though Zann didn't think he sounded very sorry.

64
00:03:19.821 --> 00:03:21.022
Ello looked dismayed.

65
00:03:21.042 --> 00:03:22.262
"Rellu, no!

66
00:03:22.562 --> 00:03:23.762
You can't turn them away."

67
00:03:23.782 --> 00:03:26.183
"You don't understand, Ello."

68
00:03:27.003 --> 00:03:28.424
The man's voice was stern.

69
00:03:28.444 --> 00:03:30.185
"Come, let's get inside."

70
00:03:31.666 --> 00:03:33.568
Most of the Skellians turned to leave.

71
00:03:33.868 --> 00:03:34.989
But Ello grabbed his mother.

72
00:03:35.009 --> 00:03:37.551
"We can't do this," he said.

73
00:03:37.571 --> 00:03:40.294
"I'm sure they're not—" "Hush, son."

74
00:03:40.614 --> 00:03:42.576
His mother shot a nervous look at the visitors.

75
00:03:42.596 --> 00:03:44.297
"What's wrong?"

76
00:03:44.717 --> 00:03:46.539
Gliss cried, her chin quivering.

77
00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:50.162
"Please! We don't understand."

78
00:03:51.203 --> 00:03:52.904
Ello's mother's expression softened.

79
00:03:53.485 --> 00:03:54.706
"Wait here," she said.

80
00:03:54.726 --> 00:03:57.952
"Let me talk to Rellu."

81
00:03:57.972 --> 00:03:59.593
She hurried off with Ello at her heels.

82
00:03:59.613 --> 00:04:01.575
"What was that all about?"

83
00:04:01.875 --> 00:04:02.476
Darb wondered.

84
00:04:03.357 --> 00:04:04.197
Zann shook his head.

85
00:04:04.217 --> 00:04:07.920
"It's like they heard Morb's name and freaked out."

86
00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:11.083
"But how would they know about Morb here?"

87
00:04:11.463 --> 00:04:11.964
Perda said.

88
00:04:11.984 --> 00:04:14.506
"Shh," Gliss shushed her.

89
00:04:14.526 --> 00:04:15.847
"Here they come."

90
00:04:16.787 --> 00:04:17.848
Ello was hurrying back.

91
00:04:18.429 --> 00:04:21.051
"I'm sorry, they're being very stubborn," he said.

92
00:04:21.071 --> 00:04:23.853
"They still won't let you stay with us.

93
00:04:24.294 --> 00:04:26.896
But they said you can stay in the old village for a few days."

94
00:04:27.888 --> 00:04:28.729
"The old village?"

95
00:04:29.069 --> 00:04:29.570
Zann said.

96
00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:31.031
"It's this way."

97
00:04:33.393 --> 00:04:34.634
Ello led them over a ridge.

98
00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:36.755
Then he pointed down a slope.

99
00:04:37.596 --> 00:04:39.417
A single hut stood at the bottom.

100
00:04:39.858 --> 00:04:42.000
The lower halves of its stilts were in the water.

101
00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:46.463
"That's where the village used to be when I was born," Ello explained.

102
00:04:46.483 --> 00:04:51.527
"The waters rose and submerged most of the houses, but that one is still out of reach of

103
00:04:51.567 --> 00:04:52.128
the gulpers.

104
00:04:52.668 --> 00:04:53.689
You'll be all right there."

105
00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:57.572
"Why did everyone get upset when we mentioned Morb?"

106
00:04:57.592 --> 00:04:58.072
Perda asked.

107
00:04:58.952 --> 00:05:01.033
Ello shrugged, looking uncomfortable.

108
00:05:01.053 --> 00:05:03.154
"I'd better go," he said.

109
00:05:03.174 --> 00:05:06.595
"The others will need my help cleaning and cooking today's catch."

110
00:05:07.415 --> 00:05:08.095
He rushed off.

111
00:05:08.115 --> 00:05:10.736
"That was weird," Darb said.

112
00:05:10.756 --> 00:05:12.236
"Never mind."

113
00:05:12.576 --> 00:05:13.356
Gliss shivered.

114
00:05:13.376 --> 00:05:15.397
"It's cold out here.

115
00:05:15.437 --> 00:05:16.537
Let's get inside."

116
00:05:18.318 --> 00:05:20.458
The hut's interior was damp and moldy.

117
00:05:21.358 --> 00:05:24.699
But Perda created a fire, and Zann conjured up some food.

118
00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:29.577
As they ate, Darb wandered onto a balcony facing the sea.

119
00:05:29.597 --> 00:05:33.479
"The gulpers are swimming near this hut now," he reported.

120
00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:35.540
"They must have sensed your magic."

121
00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:41.462
"Let's hope they can't knock the hut off its stilts," Zann joked weakly.

122
00:05:41.482 --> 00:05:44.264
"Or they might swallow us right up!"

123
00:05:45.084 --> 00:05:46.345
Perda glanced out the window.

124
00:05:46.365 --> 00:05:48.406
"It's getting darker.

125
00:05:48.966 --> 00:05:50.206
It must be almost night."

126
00:05:51.387 --> 00:05:52.287
"How can you tell?"

127
00:05:52.687 --> 00:05:53.628
Gliss grimaced.

128
00:05:54.552 --> 00:05:57.073
"The rain makes everything so gloomy all the time!

129
00:05:57.954 --> 00:06:00.896
No wonder these people want to escape to other worlds."

130
00:06:01.856 --> 00:06:02.657
Zann yawned.

131
00:06:02.677 --> 00:06:04.538
"It's been a long day.

132
00:06:05.138 --> 00:06:06.519
Let's try to get some sleep.

133
00:06:07.599 --> 00:06:09.801
Maybe we can figure out a plan tomorrow."

134
00:06:14.943 --> 00:06:20.146
Zann was in the midst of yet another confusing dream about his parents when a shout awakened him.

135
00:06:21.047 --> 00:06:23.048
His eyes popped open, and he sat up.

136
00:06:24.296 --> 00:06:25.797
Ello was standing in the doorway.

137
00:06:25.817 --> 00:06:28.399
"A storm is coming!"

138
00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:30.060
he said breathlessly.

139
00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:33.463
"Huh?" Gliss mumbled, rubbing her eyes.

140
00:06:33.483 --> 00:06:35.124
"So what?

141
00:06:35.604 --> 00:06:37.125
It never stops raining here."

142
00:06:37.145 --> 00:06:39.027
"You don't understand!"

143
00:06:39.307 --> 00:06:40.628
Ello's voice was urgent.

144
00:06:40.648 --> 00:06:42.629
"This storm is big.

145
00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:44.811
It may cause the water to rise again.

146
00:06:45.652 --> 00:06:49.594
If that happens, you'll be cut off from the shore, and at the mercy of the gulpers!"
